# platformd-verifyd user-presence verification interface.
#
# Served on a system Varlink socket at $RUNTIME_DIRECTORY/io.platformd.Verify
# (/run/platformd-verifyd/io.platformd.Verify). No secret material crosses it.
interface io.platformd.Verify

# Challenge the calling user to prove presence now by running the platformd-verify
# PAM stack, using whichever factors the administrator configured. The
# user is the caller's own (taken from the peer credentials, never a claimed
# name), so a process may only verify itself. On
# success the verification may be recorded with platformd-trustd. sessionId
# names an active, local, logind-reported unlocked user session owned by the
# caller. If it is empty, the peer process session is used, or exactly one
# eligible session is selected. An invalid explicit session is not replaced by
# another session. reason is bounded descriptive text and does not identify a
# trusted client. The PAM conversation runs in a worker and the reply arrives
# when the factor completes. One request per user may run at a time, with a
# bounded number across the machine. The request is cancelled when its client
# disconnects or the target session becomes ineligible. verified is the outcome,
# and method is the PAM service that ran.
method VerifyUser(
        sessionId: string,
        reason: string
) -> (
        verified: bool,
        method: string,
        realtimeUSec: int
)

error PermissionDenied()
error VerificationUnsupported()
error VerificationTimedOut()
error VerificationCancelled()
error PromptUnavailable()
error NoSession()
error SessionNotEligible()
error AmbiguousSession()
error Busy()
